# lfm3-1.7b-iq8r.recipe -- LiquidAI LFM3-1.7B with a rotated int8 trunk, served by lfm3_bf16.
#
#   rad-convert <LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B> -o lfm3-1.7b-iq8r.rad --recipe data/recipes/lfm3-1.7b-iq8r.recipe
#
# Every linear of the 24 layers but the attention gate (attention q, k, v and output; the
# convolutions' in and out projections; gate|up and down) becomes int8 codes in -127..127 in the
# 128-wide Hadamard domain, with a bf16 scale per [1 x 128] of K, read against int8 activations
# rotated the same way. Round to nearest with a scale search; no calibration data is read.
#
# The group is 128, not IQ8R's 256 (a u8 scale per [1 x 256] under a bf16 scale per row, as
# d1-3b-iq8r.recipe), because libhalo serves the rotated quantiser and its GEMMs at 128 only:
# this container runs on libr4d, libhalo and the host libraries. lfm3_bf16 serves the 256 form
# too, where the kernels do (libr4d, libavx, libref).
#
# Kept bf16: the attention gate (gate_proj: one row a query head, a multiplier on that whole
# head; lfm3_bf16 refuses a quantised one), the short convolution, the norms, the embedding and
# the lm_head tied to it.
blk.*.attn_q.weight          rtn  codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 clamp=sym rule=search
blk.*.attn_k.weight          rtn  codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 clamp=sym rule=search
blk.*.attn_v.weight          rtn  codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 clamp=sym rule=search
blk.*.attn_output.weight     rtn  codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 clamp=sym rule=search
blk.*.conv_in.weight         rtn  codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 clamp=sym rule=search
blk.*.conv_out.weight        rtn  codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 clamp=sym rule=search
blk.*.ffn_gate_up.weight     rtn  codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 clamp=sym rule=search
blk.*.ffn_down.weight        rtn  codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 clamp=sym rule=search
